load @term/seed/code/structure/manifold
  find manifold

# A fibration: a space that is locally a product of a base and a fiber, a way of bundling a copy of the fiber over each
# point of the base so they twist together globally. The four Hopf fibrations, one per division algebra, bundle spheres
# over spheres, and the octonionic one (the fifteen-sphere over the eight-sphere with seven-sphere fibers) is the
# topological shadow of the dimension-eight ceiling. The form carries the total manifold.
form fibration
  link space, like manifold
